cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both this implementation and the paper
  whose method it reproduces (see references below).
title: rfr-gapfill
abstract: >-
  An independent, leakage-safe Python implementation of the Random Forest Robust
  (RFR) eddy-covariance gap-filling method of Zhu et al. (2022), with explicit
  documentation of every point where the published description is ambiguous.
type: software
version: 0.1.0.dev0
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Inkenbrandt
    given-names: Paul
    email: paulinkenbrandt@gmail.com
keywords:
  - eddy covariance
  - gap filling
  - random forest
  - FLUXNET
  - carbon flux
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Stable gap-filling for longer eddy covariance data gaps: A globally
      validated machine-learning approach for carbon dioxide, water, and energy
      fluxes
    authors:
      - family-names: Zhu
        given-names: Songyan
      - family-names: Clement
        given-names: Robert
      - family-names: McCalmont
        given-names: Jon
      - family-names: Davies
        given-names: Christian A.
      - family-names: Hill
        given-names: Timothy
    journal: Agricultural and Forest Meteorology
    volume: 314
    year: 2022
    start: 108777
    doi: 10.1016/j.agrformet.2021.108777
